rostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8624},{60,"Stormcaller's Pauldrons","","Andorgos","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.  You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8602},{60,"Striker's Diadem","","Andorgos","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.  You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8657},{60,"Striker's Footguards","","Kandrostrasz","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.  This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.",8626},{60,"Striker's Hauberk","","Vethsera","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.  You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8656},{60,"Striker's Leggings","","Kandrostrasz","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8658},{60,"Striker's Pauldrons","","Andorgos","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of War, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.  You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8659},{60,"The Savior of Kalimdor","","Caelestrasz","Ahn'Qiraj","Take the Eye of C'Thun to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time.",8802},{60,"Tiara of the Oracle","","Andorgos","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.  You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8592},{60,"Trousers of the Oracle","","Kandrostrasz","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8593},{60,"Vestments of the Oracle","","Vethsera","Ahn'Qiraj","Bring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.  You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.",8603}}, stories = {["battleguard sartura"]="Battleguard Sartura is the leader of the qiraji battleguards, one of the great castes that serve the Twin Emperors. Three royal guards fight at her side.\n\nShe tells trespassers that they defile sacred ground and that the laws of the Ancients will not be challenged. They will be annihilated, she says, for she serves to the last.",["cthun"]="C'Thun is an Old God, a being of unimaginable evil and power. In the time before time, a battle between a Titan and this being raged on the soil of Silithus. A Titan fell, and the Old God fell as well, or so it was thought. For ages C'Thun lay dormant beneath the world and waited for the moment to strike back at those who had harmed it.\n\nIt reached out through the silithid and made avatars of them in its own image, the qiraji. They named their creator and spent many thousands of years building the fortress city of Ahn'Qiraj and an army to avenge him.\n\nThe night elves and the dragons walled the qiraji in a thousand years ago, but C'Thun has awakened in its lair and is regaining its power. It foresaw the dragons and cast a spell that places them under its control if they come too close. Whispers ride the winds of the Silithus desert.",["fankriss the unyielding"]="Fankriss the Unyielding is a sand reaver, a silithid that resembles a solifuge, and one of the lords of the Vekniss hive. He waits at the end of a long tunnel filled with Vekniss soldiers and drones, and more hatchlings crawl from the three tunnels around his chamber.",["ouro"]="Ouro is an ancient sand worm, a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God C'Thun himself as a mockery of life. Sand worms burrow through the soil with frightening speed and burst up beneath unwary prey.\n\nHis skin is unnaturally thick, nearly impregnable, yet flexible enough to let him move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature. He lives in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj.",["princess huhuran"]="Princess Huhuran is a large silithid wasp of the Vekniss hive, the largest hive known, behind the gates of Ahn'Qiraj. Silithid wasps are the flying attack troops of the silithid. They are very aggressive and are often found in swarms.",["silithid royalty"]="Lord Kri, Princess Yauj and Vem are silithid colossi of the Vekniss hive. It is the largest hive known, and since it lies behind the gates of Ahn'Qiraj it has grown for thousands of years with no outside interference. The three go by many names, among them the Trinity, the Triumvirate and the Bug Family.\n\nThe silithid are insects without a mind of their own. By the prophecy of the qiraji they were born from the magic of the Well of Eternity, and the qiraji were later made from them.",["the prophet skeram"]="The Prophet Skeram is a religious leader of the qiraji and the author of the Prophecy of C'Thun. He leads the prophets, one of the three great castes of the qiraji alongside the battleguards and the gladiators, and he stands guard at the entrance to the temple of Ahn'Qiraj.\n\nHis prophecy tells of a battle between a Titan and a being of unimaginable evil in the time before time. A Titan fell, and an Old God fell as well, or so it was thought. From the silithid the being made the qiraji in its own image, and they named their creator C'Thun. The record follows the war with the night elves in Silithus, and the copy that survives breaks off in Tanaris, where the qiraji face a bronze dragon.",["twin emperors"]="Vek'lor and Vek'nilash are twin brothers who rule the qiraji from the sanctuary of their temple. One works with sorcery and the other with a great sword.\n\nSince the Scarab Wall rose, the Emperors have been shut in the temple behind the barrier."} },
  [532] = { name = "Karazhan", raid = true, levels = {70,73,70}, picture = "Karazhan", where = {"Deadwind Pass",46.6,74.1}, quests = {{70,"A Demonic Presence","","Archmage Alturus","Deadwind Pass","Archmage Alturus wants you to destroy the Demonic Presence at the top of Karazhan.",9844},{70,"Nightbane","","Kalynna Lathred","Netherstorm","Go to the Master's Terrace in Karazhan and touch the Blackened Urn to summon Nightbane.  Retrieve the Faint Arcane Essence from Nightbane's corpse and bring it to Archmage Alturus.",9644},{70,"The Cudgel of Kar'desh","","Skar'this the Heretic","The Slave Pens","Skar'this the Heretic in the heroic Slave Pens of Coilfang Reservoir wants you to bring him the Earthen Signet and the Blazing Signet.",13431},{70,"The Shade of Aran","","Kamsis","Karazhan","Obtain Medivh's Journal and return to Kamsis at the Guardian's Library in Karazhan.",9640}} },
  [533] = { name = "Naxxramas", raid = true, levels = {80,83,80}, picture = "NAXXRAMAS", where = {"Dragonblight",87.5,50.6}, quests = {{60,"Echoes of War","","Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","Eastern Plaguelands","Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to slay 5 Living Monstrosities, 5 Stoneskin Gargoyles, 8 Deathknight Captains and 3 Venom Stalkers.",9033},{60,"Glacial Cloak","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 2 Essences of Water, 4 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",9237},{60,"Glacial Gloves","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 4 Essences of Water, 2 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold.",9239},{60,"Glacial Vest","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 8 Bolts of Runecloth, 6 Essences of Water, 4 Ironweb Spider Silks and 300 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",9240},{60,"Glacial Wrists","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 2 Bolts of Runecloth, 2 Essences of Water, 2 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold.",9238},{60,"Icebane Bracers","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 12 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 2 Essence of Water and 200 gold.",9235},{60,"Icebane Breastplate","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 16 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 4 Essence of Water and 300 gold. You will also need to be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",9236},{60,"Icebane Gauntlets","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 12 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 2 Essences of Water and 200 gold.",9234},{60,"Icy Scale Bracers","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 16 Heavy Scorpid Scales, 5 Essences of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.",9244},{60,"Icy Scale Breastplate","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 24 Heavy Scorpid Scale, 7 Essence of Water, 5 Cured Rugged Hides and 300 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",9246},{60,"Icy Scale Gauntlets","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 16 Heavy Scorpid Scale, 5 Essence of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.",9245},{60,"Omarion's Handbook","","Omarion's Handbook (an item)","","Take Omarion's Handbook to Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",9233},{60,"Polar Bracers","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 12 Enchanted Leather, 3 Essence of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.",9241},{60,"Polar Gloves","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 12 Enchanted Leather, 3 Essence of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.",9242},{60,"Polar Tunic","","Craftsman Wilhelm","Eastern Plaguelands","Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 16 Enchanted Leathers, 5 Essences of Water, 5 Cured Rugged Hides and 300 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",9243},{60,"Redemption Headpiece","","Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","Eastern Plaguelands","Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Redemption Headpiece if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Headpiece, 15 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 5 Arcanite Bars and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.",9045},{60,"The Fall of Kel'Thuzad","","The Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad (an item)","","Take the Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad to Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",9120},{80,"Anub'Rekhan Must Die!","","Archmage Lan'dalock","Dalaran","Kill Anub'Rekhan.\n\nThis quest can be completed with any difficulty or size raid.",24580},{80,"Instructor Razuvious Must Die!","","Archmage Lan'dalock","Dalaran","Kill Instructor Razuvious.\n\nThis quest can be completed with any difficulty or size raid.",24582},{80,"Noth the Plaguebringer Must Die!","","Archmage Lan'dalock","Dalaran","Kill Noth the Plaguebringer.\n\nThis quest can be completed with any difficulty or size raid.",24581},{80,"Patchwerk Must Die!","","Archmage Lan'dalock","Dalaran","Kill Patchwerk.\n\nThis quest can be completed with any difficulty or size raid.",24583}}, stories = {["anubrekhan"]="Anub'Rekhan was one of the finest spider lords of Azjol'Nerub, the underground kingdom of the nerubians. When the Lich King broke that kingdom, the crypt lords were swayed to his side and given the long servitude of undeath. Anub'Rekhan was brought under Scourge control when he and his commander, Anub'arak, were defeated, and it is said that he was the most loyal of Anub'arak's commanders.\n\nNow the crypt lord guards the doors of the Spider Wing in Naxxramas. He greets visitors with a mock-polite welcome to his parlor. He speaks of the hearts he hears beating and of the blood he has gone too long without.",["gluth"]="The undead plague-dog Gluth sits obediently within Naxxramas, waiting for orders from his masters. His appetite is so great that even the living were not enough to feed it.\n\nIt is rumored that Feugen feeds him an army of zombies every day. Gluth uses them to knit his own decaying flesh back together, and in this way the remains of undead too weak to fight are put to use.",["gothik the harvester"]="Gothik the Harvester is a necromancer, a master of necromancy and conjuration. He is said to be able to call forth legions of the undead at a moment's notice, and it is with his guidance that even the weakest death knights learn to raise the dead.\n\nHe serves Kel'Thuzad in the Military Quarter of Naxxramas.",["grand widow faerlina"]="Grand Widow Faerlina was a botanist in life, and later one of the high-ranking members of the Cult of the Damned under Kel'Thuzad. Death did not end her service. In Naxxramas she oversees the Spider Wing, breeding and tending the seemingly endless swarms of arachnids that crawl out of the citadel's depths.\n\nShe is a master of poisons and has a keen understanding of what makes mortals suffer. The venoms she brews for the Lich King come from the spiderlings that Maexxna produces.",["grobbulus"]="Grobbulus is a flesh giant, the first successful one of its kind. The same plague slime that flows through Naxxramas runs inside his hulking body.\n\nHe was made to help build an army that could spread the undead plague quickly. His makers meant to inject the living ooze into the bodies of their foes. The recipient of such an injection would usually flee to his allies and bring them down with him.",["heigan the unclean"]="Heigan the Unclean was the mastermind behind the magic of the plague cauldrons, which spread the undead plague through Lordaeron so quickly. The sickness corrupted the plants and animals of the countryside along with the human population. The whole wilderness around Lordaeron is now called the Plaguelands, thanks in no small part to Heigan's handiwork.\n\nWithin Naxxramas he is said to have rigged the walls and floors of the citadel with a vast array of traps, which he can spring at will.",["instructor razuvious"]="Instructor Razuvious is the most feared of the death knight trainers of the Scourge. Kel'Thuzad appointed him to train all death knights, and it is said that his technique is so potent that only a disciple of his could hope to withstand him.\n\nIn Naxxramas he holds his post in the Military Quarter, and a company of Death Knight Understudies stands with him.",["kelthuzad"]="Kel'Thuzad was an archmage of the Kirin Tor and a member of the Council of Six in Dalaran. His interest in the dark arts cost him his rank and holdings, and Grand Magus Antonidas exiled him. Driven by a voice in his head, he traveled to Northrend and climbed the Frozen Throne to offer his soul to the Lich King.\n\nAs a necromancer of the Scourge he came back to Lordaeron and founded the Cult of the Damned in secret, recruiting among nobles and commoners with promises of immortality. Through the cult he became one of the Lich King's principal agents in spreading the plague of undeath across Lordaeron. Arthas Menethil killed him, then raised him again as a lich, and in the Third War Kel'Thuzad summoned the demon lord Archimonde into the world.\n\nWhen Arthas sailed for Northrend, he left Kel'Thuzad to command the Scourge in Lordaeron. From the floating necropolis of Naxxramas he rules the Eastern Plaguelands and fights the Scarlet Crusade, the Argent Dawn, the Alliance and the Horde.",["loatheb"]="Loatheb shows what the plague did to the living things of the land. He is a twisted fen creeper, the hideous result of fusing the living plague with the bog beasts of Azeroth.\n\nThe plant kingdom can regrow what is cut from it, and in Loatheb that gift is mocked. He summons deadly spores that spread a sickening miasma, and he is said to control the power of healing itself, turning the healing arts against those who wield them.",["maexxna"]="Maexxna is a massive spider, taken from the depths of Northrend's mountains many ages ago. She was captured within the dread citadel Naxxramas, and there she gives birth to her brood.\n\nShe feasts on those foolish enough to enter the necropolis and feeds her spawn with their corpses. Spider after spider comes of it, and Kel'Thuzad turns them to his own foul ends. Even the poisons of Grand Widow Faerlina are drawn from Maexxna's spiderlings.",["noth the plaguebringer"]="Noth the Plaguebringer was once a respected mage of Dalaran. He heard the call of the Lich King in much the same way Kel'Thuzad did, and like Kel'Thuzad he was driven by hunger for power. He accepted the summons and gave the Scourge his skill in necromancy and curse-weaving.\n\nThe Third War troubled him. As it took the lives of countless innocents, Noth began to doubt his choice and to doubt Kel'Thuzad. Kel'Thuzad answered that growing compassion quickly, by freezing the living heart in Noth's chest. Noth now serves on in Naxxramas.",["patchwerk"]="Patchwerk is a titanic abomination, stitched together from the dead, and Kel'Thuzad calls him his Avatar of War. He is one of the most powerful abominations the necromancer has made. Abominations are slow and dull-witted by reputation, which is why the tales of his strength and speed were so hard to believe. Patchwerk is neither slow nor mindless, and he uses his great power to pulverize anyone who stands against him with a flurry of heavy blows.\n\nHe has little to say for himself. In Naxxramas he greets intruders with the simple cry that Patchwerk wants to play.",["sapphiron"]="Sapphiron was one of the most ancient dragons of the blue flight and had immense magical power. He lived with his brood in the mountains of Northrend near the entrance to Azjol-Nerub, guarding a hoard of artifacts gathered over the centuries. When Arthas and the nerubian Anub'arak set out through Azjol-Nerub toward Icecrown, they sought that hoard. Sapphiron met them, and found it refreshing that Arthas was so frank about killing him and taking his treasure. The Scourge killed the wyrm and his dragons, and Arthas raised Sapphiron as a frost wyrm.\n\nYears later the frost wyrm stands guard in Naxxramas, over the chamber of its master Kel'Thuzad. His power has been sharpened by his rebirth, and he uses frost to defend the lich at all costs.",["thaddius"]="Thaddius is a massive abomination pieced together from the flesh of innocent women and children. He dwells in one of the experimental laboratories of Naxxramas, a vast hall of strange machinery where powerful bolts of electricity arc through the air and paint the walls with jagged shadows. The current charges Thaddius and the two huge wights that flank him, Stalagg and Feugen.\n\nIt is said that the souls contained in Thaddius are fused together, eternally bound within that foul prison of flesh.",["the four horsemen"]="The Four Horsemen are death knights, made by Kel'Thuzad to serve as his royal guard. The most feared soldiers of the Scourge, they are his greatest creation, and they are linked to the lich so closely that only his destruction truly ends them. Thane Korth'azz, a dwarf, wields the power of flame and can call fiery meteors from the sky. Lady Blaumeux is a master of shadow, able to drain the essence of life from those she meets. Sir Zeliek served the Order of the Silver Hand while he lived, and his faith was so strong that the Light still answers him in undeath. His body must obey Kel'Thuzad, yet he has kept his sanity and his morals, and the work he is forced to do is a torment.\n\nHighlord Alexandros Mograine leads them. He was a hero of the Alliance of Lordaeron and the first wielder of the Ashbringer. After his fall Kel'Thuzad took his body, broke his will and set him at the head of the Horsemen. Together they oversee the Military Quarter of Naxxramas."} },
  [534] = { name = "The Battle for Mount Hyjal", raid = true, levels = {70,73,70}, picture = "HyjalPast", where = {"Tanaris",57.1,49.6}, quests = {{70,"An Artifact From the Past","","Akama","Shadowmoon Valley","Go to the Caverns of Time in Tanaris and gain access to the Battle of Mount Hyjal.  Once inside, defeat Rage Winterchill and bring the Time-Phased Phylactery to Akama in Shadowmoon Valley.",10947}} },
